@startuml

title Versions packages
caption All packages and their dependencies are [[https://www.archunit.org/{What is ArchUnit?} ArchUnit]]-tested against the code
footer docs/architecture/versions-packages.puml

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam hyperlinkColor #1A4FA0
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
' the box label is the package pattern itself, which ArchUnit reads from the stereotype;
' the stereotype is hidden so the pattern is not printed twice
hide stereotype
skinparam ranksep 30
<style>
component {
  BackGroundColor #ECEFF1
  LineColor #546E7A
}
arrow {
  LineColor #78909C
}
</style>

' A box is a package directly under versions and its subpackages (<<..porthole.versions.x..>>); [..versions] is the
' slice's root package alone. An arrow is a dependency the code has: PackagesArchTest fails on one the code has and
' this file does not draw, and on one drawn here that the code lacks. Dependencies on other slices and on shared are
' not drawn; the C3 view has those. A root never depends on its own adapters (ArchitectureTest), so every arrow
' between an adapter and the root points at the root.

[..versions.registry] <<..porthole.versions.registry..>>
[..versions.web] <<..porthole.versions.web..>>
[..versions] <<..porthole.versions>>

[..versions.registry] --> [..versions]
[..versions.web] --> [..versions]

@enduml
